509	     * gap note: none of the original 9 table cases exercised a climb of
510	     * more than one ancestor. Random search + delta-debug shrinking (over
511	     * an instrumented scratch copy of delete_fixup, never src/rbtree.c
512	     * itself) found this is genuinely hard to produce small -- no sequence
513	     * under 38 nodes reproduces two real climbing passes; every insertion
514	     * permutation tried at n<38 either never reached delete_fixup's loop
515	     * body twice or resolved by the second level. Traced against the real
516	     * compiled rb_delete (case labels added via fprintf instrumentation,
517	     * no logic changed):
518	     *   iter1: x=NIL,   parent=00028(B) -> Case 3 (sib=00029, both nephews
519	     *          NIL) -> sib recolored RED, x=00028, parent=00026 (CLIMBS,
520	     *          since 00028 was black -- nothing to absorb the debt yet)
521	     *   iter2: x=00028, parent=00026(B) -> Case 3 mirror (sib=00023, both
522	     *          nephews black) -> sib recolored RED, x=00026, parent=00021
